WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.740
- All right, I wanna close things out

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:02.670
with one more highlight

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.470
from our season four premier road trip.

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.739
This is "What I'm Liking".

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:07.000
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.970
(audience applauds)

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.100
Two weeks ago, we rolled
into New York city,

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.870
with our recording studio on wheels

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.040
to kick off our search

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.290
for the country's greatest
undiscovered voices.

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:19.350
That first day was filled
with excitement and surprises.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.900
Our friends at the "Today"
show got in on the fun as well.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.850
They featured some people in the crowd,

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.950
waiting to sing on our Kellyoke bus.

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:28.620
But one guest, an aspiring
singer named Jade,

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.030
had no idea I was there.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.029
It was awesome.

00:00:31.029 --> 00:00:32.398
(swooshing)

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:35.599
♪ Since you've been gone ♪

00:00:35.599 --> 00:00:36.432
(audience applauds)

00:00:36.432 --> 00:00:40.160
♪ I can breathe for the first time ♪

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:44.371
♪ I'm so moving on, yeah, yeah ♪

00:00:44.371 --> 00:00:46.379
♪ Thanks to you ♪

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.029
♪ Now I get ♪

00:00:48.029 --> 00:00:50.531
♪ I get what I want ♪

00:00:50.531 --> 00:00:55.531
(audience applauds)
(Jade screams)

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:02.029
I am totally stealing that
run, that run, I was like...

00:01:02.029 --> 00:01:02.862
(Kelly screams)

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:04.971
I walked out, I was like,
"Wait, what was so good".

00:01:04.971 --> 00:01:06.643
(audience applauds)

00:01:06.643 --> 00:01:08.373
I love a good surprise,

00:01:08.373 --> 00:01:10.590
when I am the one doing the surprising.

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:13.020
We have Jade on the line right now.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:14.281
What's up, Jade?

00:01:14.281 --> 00:01:16.461
(audience applauds)

00:01:16.461 --> 00:01:18.133
- Hi, everybody, hi, Kelly.

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:20.190
- It's great to see you again.

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:22.290
So, was it a good surprise?

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:23.541
- A good surprise?

00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:24.374
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:24.374 --> 00:01:25.965
A great surprise, actually.

00:01:25.965 --> 00:01:27.300
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:28.341
- [Kelly] Well, wait, well...

00:01:28.341 --> 00:01:30.360
- [Jade] It was such a
special moment, Kelly.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:31.740
I remember when I was younger,

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:35.940
my parents got me a karaoke
machine with one singular CD

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:38.421
and it literally, the first song on the CD

00:01:38.421 --> 00:01:41.021
was "Stronger" by Kelly Clarkson.

00:01:41.021 --> 00:01:41.854
- Yes.

00:01:41.854 --> 00:01:43.770
- [Jade] And just to know
that you are a part of

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.830
some of my earliest memories in music,

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.360
is just so special to me.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.820
And the moment I will cherish forever,

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.253
especially when you complimented my run.

00:01:53.253 --> 00:01:54.086
(audience laughs)

00:01:54.086 --> 00:01:56.790
- Oh, I'm not lying either, I'm taking it.

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:59.940
I was like, "Oh, okay,
wait, that was really nice".

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:02.040
Well, I, we got to talk a little bit,

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:03.330
but everybody else doesn't know

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:04.770
like, your like, you know, aspiration.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:06.510
So, tell everybody what you wanna do.

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:08.520
- Right, so, right now I'm in an era

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.190
where I'm really finding myself in music.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:15.120
I'm actually studying classical
music at NYU right now.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:16.020
- Wow.

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:19.740
- So, I really appreciate you
as a cross genre vocalist,

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.930
shout out to the Kellyoke album.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:24.720
Not a lot of people can
go from "Blue Bayou"

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.460
to "Call Out My Name".

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.760
Shout out to you for that.
(Jade chuckles)

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:29.593
- [Kelly] Oh, my God, love you.

00:02:29.593 --> 00:02:31.502
You're making me feel really
good about myself, what?

00:02:31.502 --> 00:02:32.430
(audience chuckles)

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:33.750
But you know what, you would know though,

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.880
like if you learn, if
you're classically trained

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.500
it is easier to kind of, you know,

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:38.880
be fluid through different genres

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.770
and we all love all
different kinds of music.

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:41.820
- Right, yeah.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.500
I definitely agree with that.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:46.860
And as we spoke before, I
mentioned to you that I'd love

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:48.360
to be a music educator.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.193
- Yeah.

00:02:49.193 --> 00:02:53.190
- And yeah, just to spread
the joy that I have of music

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:56.250
with other people, especially
with younger people,

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:58.680
it would just make me
feel so accomplished.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:01.260
So, very appreciative for you.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.420
- I love you, Jade.
(audience applauds)

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:04.587
I love you so much.

00:03:04.587 --> 00:03:06.660
I'm so glad that we met

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.022
and I'm liking your post
right now, right, ma'am?

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.050
(bell rings)

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:11.531
- [Jade] Thank you.

00:03:11.531 --> 00:03:12.364
(audience applauds)

00:03:12.364 --> 00:03:13.440
- All right, well that's not all,

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.300
our season-long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.760
makers of G2, the go to pen
of the "Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.190
want to honor truly unstoppable people,

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:21.240
just like you, ma'am,

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:22.800
so they're gonna write you a check

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:25.091
for $1,000 to aid in
whatever you wanna do.

00:03:25.091 --> 00:03:26.611
(audience applauds)

00:03:26.611 --> 00:03:28.470
- Oh, my goodness, oh, my God.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:29.529
Thank you so much.

00:03:29.529 --> 00:03:30.592
(audience applauds)

00:03:30.592 --> 00:03:31.843
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:03:31.843 --> 00:03:33.330
Good luck, Jade.

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.010
We love you at the "Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:36.840
and thank you to all
of our guests this hour

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.040
and to each and every person

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.330
who made this two-week premier road trip

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:42.510
utterly spectacular, thank you.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:43.860
It has been an amazing time

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.750
and there're so many
more good times to come

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:47.550
throughout all of season four.

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:48.900
So, keep on watching, everybody.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:51.563
Meanwhile, have a great
day and a great weekend

00:03:51.563 --> 00:03:54.090
and if not, well, try and change it.

